@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Class structure — Accept a request
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
hide empty members

class AcceptRequestCommand {
  +Guid RequestId
}
class AcceptRequestCommandHandler {
  +Handle(AcceptRequestCommand) : AcceptRequestResult
}
class AcceptRequestResult {
  +Guid RequestId
  +Guid ThreadId
}
class ListingRequest {
  +Guid Id
  +Guid ListingId
  +Guid RequesterId
  +RequestStatus Status
  +byte[] RowVersion
  +Accept() : void
  +Decline() : void
}
note bottom of ListingRequest
  RowVersion is checked on save.
  Accept and decline racing resolve
  to one winner and one 409.
end note
enum RequestStatus {
  Pending
  Accepted
  Declined
}
class MessageThread {
  +Guid Id
  +Guid RequestId
  +Guid ListingId
  +Guid OwnerId
  +Guid RequesterId
  +DateTimeOffset OpenedOn
}
note bottom of MessageThread
  RequestId is unique, so one
  accepted request opens exactly
  one thread even under a race.
end note
class RequestAlreadyDecidedException {
  +Guid RequestId
  +RequestStatus CurrentStatus
}

AcceptRequestCommandHandler ..> AcceptRequestCommand : handles
AcceptRequestCommandHandler --> AcceptRequestResult : returns
AcceptRequestCommandHandler --> ListingRequest : loads and mutates
AcceptRequestCommandHandler --> MessageThread : creates
ListingRequest --> RequestStatus : holds
ListingRequest ..> RequestAlreadyDecidedException : raises on a second decision
MessageThread --> ListingRequest : opened by exactly one
@enduml
